<title>USA: DLJ expands fixed income research staff.</title>
<headline>DLJ expands fixed income research staff.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Donaldson, Lufkin &amp; Jenrette, Inc said on Monday James F. Titus Jr. has joined the firm as a Director of Real Estate Debt Securities Research in the Fixed Income Research Division.</p>
<p>Prior to joining DLJ, Titus, 35, was the Managing Director of the Real Estate Finance Group at McGraw-Hill Cos Inc's Standard &amp; Poor's Corp. During his 10 years at Standard &amp; Poor's, Titus developed much of the criteria used to evaluate and rate commercial mortgage-backed securities.</p>
<p>((-- New York Newsdesk 212-859-1610.))</p>
